       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would make the effects hard to reverse.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum dose. It's often used after titrating up from 5 mg.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is sometimes used in frail or elderly patients, or with hepatic impairment. It doesn't apply here, since your patient has normal liver function.\n\nIf 50 mg is deliberate, please tell me the clinical rationale and I'll reconsider. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
